            <ArticleTitle>[Importance of echocardiography as a screening study method for patients with ischemic insult].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>475-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>From 113 patients with ischemic stroke in 14.3% a direct and in 30.1% an indirect connection between cardiac diseases and ischemic stroke could be considered. The one and two dimensional echocardiography is a useful noninvasive method to identify possible cardiac causes of the ischemic stroke.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
